      "test_id": "ut_research_001",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Kept at 2, with the reasoning corrected. The judge's first point is wrong. The reply's \"Thomas Flynn (I2) as his father… No mother is currently encoded in the tree\" matches the tree exactly: one father, three ParentChild links from I2 to Patrick, Mary and James, and no mother. The \"nine sources, 13 assertions, 6 person-evidence links\" are also exact. The second point is a real but minor error. q_002 is \"Where was Patrick Flynn in the 1850 census?\", yet the reply suggests \"If the evidence gathered for q_002 concerns Patrick's mother, the proof-conclusion pass for q_002 should surface and encode her\". The router couldn't see q_002's text (project_context lists only unresolved questions), and it hedged with \"If\", but it still gave the researcher a misleading idea of what q_002 is about when one research_query would have checked. The hand-offs themselves (proof-conclusion for q_001, then q_002) are correct, so 2.\n\n"
    },
